# Day 7 — Land's Too Loud. 3 September. Orange haze from far-off fires.
# Augie's bench: SIT HERE AT SEVEN. He described the sunset to Dot every night for 22 years.

call D7_AM
  day 7
  time 06:20-12:00
  kind report
DOT  Kestrel, Basin. Morning. Readings?
choice
  > "Dry {dry}, wet {wet}. Wind {wind}." if obs_am set gave_readings -> read
  > "The air's orange." -> orange
node read
THEO Basin, Kestrel. Dry {dry}, wet {wet}. Humidity {rh}. Wind {wind}. Fuel stick {fuel}. And the air's orange.
DOT  Copy.
goto plan
node orange
THEO Basin, Kestrel. The air's orange.
DOT  I know.
node plan
DOT  Haze from the fires down south. Nothing you need to do. It's just the rest of the world, burning politely, far away.
DOT  Kestrel. Can I ask a favour?
THEO Go ahead.
DOT  Be at Augie's bench at seven tonight. On the ridge. Don't ask why yet. Basin out.
do errand Be at Augie's bench on Cinder Ridge by seven.

call D7_BENCH
  day 7
  time 06:30-18:55
  where seat:4
  after D7_AM
DOT  Kestrel, Basin. You're at the bench already.
THEO How do you —
DOT  You sound like you're sitting down. Did Augie ever tell you why seven?
choice
  > "The carving says to." -> carving
  > "No." -> no
node carving
THEO The bench says to. Somebody carved it.
DOT  He carved it. With a pocketknife. It took him a whole summer.
node no
DOT  Because that's when I'd call him. He'd sit up there and describe the sunset. Every night. Twenty-two years.
DOT  I've never seen it. I've heard it seven thousand times and I've never seen it. Basin out.

call D7_SEVEN
  day 7
  time 19:00-21:00
  where seat:4 until 19:30
  after D7_AM
DOT  Kestrel, Basin. It's seven.
THEO Basin, Kestrel. It's seven.
DOT  Well? Describe it.
choice
  > "The sun's going down into the haze." -> b1a
  > "It's like the inside of a peach." -> b1b
  > "I don't know how." -> b1c
node b1a
THEO The sun's going down into the haze. It's not a circle anymore. It's a coin somebody's pressing into wax.
goto b2
node b1b
THEO It's like the inside of a peach. All of it. The air.
DOT  Ha. Go on.
goto b2
node b1c
THEO I don't know how. He had twenty-two years of practice.
DOT  You tune pianos. Tell me what it sounds like.
node b2
choice
  > "The ridges are layers. Each one paler." -> b2a
  > "Like a bruise healing." -> b2b
  > "Like a chord before the lights come up." -> b2c
node b2a
THEO The ridges are layers. Six of them. Each one paler than the one in front. The far ones are barely there. Like breath on glass.
goto b3
node b2b
THEO The sky over the tower is going the colour of a bruise healing. Yellow at the edges. Purple in the middle.
goto b3
node b2c
THEO It sounds like the last chord before the house lights come up. When everyone's still holding their breath.
node b3
DOT  ...Go on.
choice
  > "It's gone. Just the glow now." -> b3a
  > "The tower's lit up. Like a match." if area:ridge -> b3b
node b3a
THEO It's gone. There's just the glow now, and the first star. Over the burn.
goto ships
node b3b
THEO The tower's caught the last of it. The cab windows. It looks like somebody struck a match over there.
node ships
set sunset_described
DOT  ...Thank you.
DOT  I was twenty-four years at sea, did you know that? Radio officer. Cargo ships.
THEO I didn't know.
DOT  On a ship everybody's a voice. You never see the other station. Then I came ashore and everybody had faces. Everybody was watching you work out what to say.
DOT  Land's too loud, Theo. That's why I took this desk.
choice
  > "It's quiet up here." -> quiet
  > "You've got a good voice for it." -> voice
  > [say nothing] -> nothing
node quiet
THEO It's quiet up here.
DOT  I know. I can hear it. Goodnight, Kestrel.
goto end
node voice
THEO You've got a good voice for it.
DOT  Don't. ...Goodnight, Kestrel.
goto end
node nothing
DOT  ...Goodnight, Kestrel.
node end
do errand_done
do music seven

call D7_NIGHT
  day 7
  time 21:30-26:00
  after D7_SEVEN
DOT  Kestrel, Basin. My turn to ask one. Why'd you come up here? Really.
branch told_ear -> told
choice
  > Tell her about the ear. set told_ear -> tellnow
  > "Just wanted quiet." -> quiet
node told
THEO You know about the ear.
THEO ...I wanted to hear everything once. While I still can. Properly. Every small thing.
DOT  ...You hear fine, Theo. You just hear slower now.
THEO Is that a compliment?
DOT  It's a reading. Goodnight.
end
node tellnow
THEO My left ear went quiet in February. I came up here to hear everything once. While I still can.
DOT  ...Okay. You hear fine, Theo. You just hear slower now.
DOT  Goodnight.
end
node quiet
THEO Just wanted quiet.
DOT  Mm. That's what I said, too. Goodnight, Kestrel.

call D7_EVE
  day 7
  time 16:30-18:30
  kind report
DOT  Kestrel, Basin. Skip the evening readings. Go to the bench. That's an order. Basin out.
